[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629454794","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102323#issuecomment-2629454794","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102323","id":2629454794,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cukvK","user":{"login":"quinnyo","id":3379314,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNzkzMTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3379314?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/quinnyo","html_url":"https://github.com/quinnyo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quinnyo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quinnyo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quinnyo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quinnyo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quinnyo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quinnyo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quinnyo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quinnyo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quinnyo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-02T16:07:34Z","updated_at":"2025-02-02T16:07:34Z","body":"This isn't a bug, in my opinion.\n\nThe observable effect (angular acceleration/velocity) of some torque on a body is entirely dependent on the moment of inertia, and the moment of inertia is derived from the body's mass and arrangement of collision shapes.\nDisabling a collision shape effectively removes it from the body, and the moment of inertia is presumably getting updated (correctly) to zero when that happens.\nZero inertia means zero acceleration as rigid body physics equations make the assumption that bodies have mass/inertia. Applying the torque would involve a divide-by-zero.\n\nLinear forces continue to work with no collision shapes because the mass is a required parameter of the body itself, which is arguably unrealistic but most physics engines just work this way. The moment of inertia is also a parameter of the body -- just one that is (by default) automatically calculated.\n\nAs a suggestion, you might try other means to temporarily disable collisions, like removing the body from certain layers.\nOtherwise, you can override the automatically calculated moment of inertia with the `RigidBody2D.inertia` property.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2629454794/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2630789821","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102323#issuecomment-2630789821","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102323","id":2630789821,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6czqq9","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-03T12:18:40Z","updated_at":"2025-02-03T12:18:40Z","body":"This is already [documented as a limitation](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_rigidbody2d.html#class-rigidbody2d-method-apply-torque), you need to set the intertia manually","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2630789821/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2630846973","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102323#issuecomment-2630846973","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102323","id":2630846973,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cz4n9","user":{"login":"ulfben","id":5237741,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMzc3NDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5237741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfben","html_url":"https://github.com/ulfben","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfben/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfben/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfben/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfben/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfben/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfben/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfben/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfben/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfben/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-03T12:44:28Z","updated_at":"2025-02-03T12:44:28Z","body":"Thank you for investigating this issue and providing the documentation link (and thanks for the physics explanation, @quinnyo)!\n\nI'll reference your response in the original issue, as I expect many others following the book will encounter and search for this problem.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2630846973/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]